Igloo's fixes for Jellyfin's tonemap_cuda filter (patches 0002-0004).
Applies on top of them; FFmpeg code under the LGPL, like the files it patches.

- filter_frame kept a failed kernel launch or output buffer allocation from
  reaching the caller (cuCtxPopCurrent's result overwrote it) and passed an
  empty frame downstream. It now fails the graph, always pops the context it
  pushed, and reports a failed Dolby Vision remap allocation as ENOMEM
  instead of dropping the frame silently.
- compile no longer leaks the Dolby Vision parameter buffers and the 3D LUT
  when it runs again after the input color properties change.
- A recompile no longer frees the dither texture, which only config_props
  creates: dithering stayed off after a switch to Dolby Vision frames.
- A Dolby Vision frame whose L1 (or L0) peak is 0 no longer yields a peak of
  0, which made the tone curve divide by zero.

Index: FFmpeg/libavfilter/colorspace.c
===================================================================
--- FFmpeg.orig/libavfilter/colorspace.c
+++ FFmpeg/libavfilter/colorspace.c
@@ -217,11 +217,12 @@
     color = av_dovi_get_color(data);
     // L0 max
     peak = color->source_max_pq / 4095.0f;
-    // L1 max
-    if (!l0_only && (ext = av_dovi_find_level(data, 1)))
+    // L1 max, when the scene carries one
+    if (!l0_only && (ext = av_dovi_find_level(data, 1)) && ext->l1.max_pq)
         peak = ext->l1.max_pq / 4095.0f;
+    // No usable peak: fall back like untagged metadata does, never return 0
     if (!peak)
-        return peak;
+        return 100.0f;
 
     peak = powf(peak, 1.0f / ST2084_M2);
     peak = FFMAX(peak - ST2084_C1, 0.0f) / FFMAX((ST2084_C2 - ST2084_C3 * peak), FLOAT_EPS);
